WEBVTT
NOTE OpenIE Research TV v3.0 — satb-harness (45s) Narrator Mia

1
00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:03.346
First, changing the wrapper around an AI model

2
00:00:03.346 --> 00:00:06.478
can swing scores as much as swapping the model.

3
00:00:06.918 --> 00:00:11.266
Second, this test harness locks prompts, memory trimming,

4
00:00:11.266 --> 00:00:14.927
and tools so every AI takes the exact same exam.

5
00:00:15.367 --> 00:00:17.706
Third, across five computer types,

6
00:00:17.706 --> 00:00:23.486
it separates real board sensors from chip counters and blocks noisy power estimates.

7
00:00:23.926 --> 00:00:30.641
Giving the exact same language model a different command wrapper shifted coding scores by seventeen points,

8
00:00:30.641 --> 00:00:36.477
while popular cloud tools that split server power by CPU share erred by up to ninety percent.

9
00:00:36.917 --> 00:00:41.743
Locking the wrapper in Rust and labeling board sensors separately from chip

10
00:00:41.743 --> 00:00:48.048
counters makes model comparisons genuinely reproducible across macOS, Linux, and Windows machines.
